{
  "id": "d300bbb8-00ab-499b-99e3-e5b6635095cd",
  "page_title": "use-your-data-go",
  "page_description": "",
  "page_date": "03/07/2024",
  "chunk_title": "Create the Go app",
  "chunk_content": "Create the Go app  1. From the project directory, open the *sample.go* file and add the following code:     ```golang    package main     import (    \t\"context\"    \t\"fmt\"    \t\"log\"    \t\"os\"        \t\"github.com/Azure/azure-sdk-for-go/sdk/ai/azopenai\"    \t\"github.com/Azure/azure-sdk-for-go/sdk/azcore\"    \t\"github.com/Azure/azure-sdk-for-go/sdk/azcore/to\"    )        func main() {    \tazureOpenAIKey := os.Getenv(\"AZURE_OPENAI_API_KEY\")    \tmodelDeploymentID := os.Getenv(\"AZURE_OPENAI_DEPLOYMENT_ID\")        \t// Ex: \"https://<your-azure-openai-host>.openai.azure.com\"    \tazureOpenAIEndpoint := os.Getenv(\"AZURE_OPENAI_ENDPOINT\")        \t// Azure AI Search configuration    \tsearchIndex := os.Getenv(\"AZURE_AI_SEARCH_INDEX\")    \tsearchEndpoint := os.Getenv(\"AZURE_AI_SEARCH_ENDPOINT\")    \tsearchAPIKey := os.Getenv(\"AZURE_AI_SEARCH_API_KEY\")        \tif azureOpenAIKey == \"\" || modelDeploymentID == \"\" || azureOpenAIEndpoint == \"\" || searchIndex == \"\" || searchEndpoint == \"\" || searchAPIKey == \"\" {    \t\tfmt.Fprintf(os.Stderr, \"Skipping example, environment variables missing\\n\")    \t\treturn    \t}        \tkeyCredential := azcore.NewKeyCredential(azureOpenAIKey)        \t// In Azure OpenAI you must deploy a model before you can use it in your client. For more information    \t// see here: https://learn.microsoft.com/azure/cognitive-services/openai/how-to/create-resource    \tclient, err := azopenai.NewClientWithKeyCredential(azureOpenAIEndpoint, keyCredential, nil)        \tif err != nil {    \t\t//  TODO: Update the following line with your application specific error handling logic    \t\tlog.Fatalf(\"ERROR: %s\", err)    \t}        \tresp, err := client.GetChatCompletions(context.TODO(), azopenai.ChatCompletionsOptions{    \t\tMessages: []azopenai.ChatRequestMessageClassification{    \t\t\t&azopenai.ChatRequestUserMessage{Content: azopenai.NewChatRequestUserMessageContent(\"What are my available health plans?\")},    \t\t},    \t\tMaxTokens: to.Ptrint32,    \t\tAzureExtensionsOptions: []azopenai.AzureChatExtensionConfigurationClassification{    \t\t\t&azopenai.AzureCognitiveSearchChatExtensionConfiguration{    \t\t\t\t// This allows Azure OpenAI to use an Azure AI Search index.    \t\t\t\t//    \t\t\t\t// > Because the model has access to, and can reference specific sources to support its responses, answers are not only based on its pretrained knowledge    \t\t\t\t// > but also on the latest information available in the designated data source. This grounding data also helps the model avoid generating responses    \t\t\t\t// > based on outdated or incorrect information.    \t\t\t\t//    \t\t\t\t// Quote from here: https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/azure/ai-services/openai/concepts/use-your-data    \t\t\t\tParameters: &azopenai.AzureCognitiveSearchChatExtensionParameters{    \t\t\t\t\tEndpoint:  &searchEndpoint,    \t\t\t\t\tIndexName: &searchIndex,    \t\t\t\t\tAuthentication: &azopenai.OnYourDataAPIKeyAuthenticationOptions{    \t\t\t\t\t\tKey: &searchAPIKey,    \t\t\t\t\t},    \t\t\t\t},    \t\t\t},    \t\t},    \t\tDeploymentName: &modelDeploymentID,    \t}, nil)        \tif err != nil {    \t\t//  TODO: Update the following line with your application specific error handling logic    \t\tlog.Fatalf(\"ERROR: %s\", err)    \t}        \t// Contains contextual information from your Azure chat completion extensions, configured above in `AzureExtensionsOptions`    \tmsgContext := resp.Choices[0].Message.Context        \tfmt.Fprintf(os.Stderr, \"Extensions Context Role: %s\\nExtensions Context (length): %d\\n\",    \t\t*msgContext.Messages[0].Role,    \t\tlen(*msgContext.Messages[0].Content))        \tfmt.Fprintf(os.Stderr, \"ChatRole: %s\\nChat content: %s\\n\",    \t\t*resp.Choices[0].Message.Role,    \t\t*resp.Choices[0].Message.Content,    \t)    }    ```     > [!IMPORTANT]    > For production, use a secure way of storing and accessing your credentials like Azure Key Vault. For more information about credential security, see the Azure AI services security article.  1. Execute the following command:     ```cmd    go run sample.go    ```     The application prints the response including both answers to your query and citations from your uploaded files.  > [!div class=\"nextstepaction\"] > I ran into an issue when running the code samples.",
